David I hear often that the country is  more divided than ever but it's divided  for a good reason  one side is insane is it really that bad  for the country to be divided I think  it's important to answer this question  to understand that partisanship and  division are two different things and  I'm not saying the country isn't divided  but divided might point more towards the  types of circumstances that would lead  to a civil war right where half the  country wants to separate the south  wants to secede in order to maintain  states rights to have slavery be legal  for example we don't have that level of  division right now there are some  secessionist but not that many a lot of  us who say hey the red states want to  bail go ahead we are the financially  viable blue states we're sort of joking  I mean it would be extraordinarily  damaging to the country if the country  were to separate into financially even  if mathematically in the long run the  blue states would be fine and the red  states wouldn't it would be such a jolt  to the system that it would be very bad  for the economy for a while the  partisanship we are seeing is partially  because we are sort of coming to a  potentially big change in the path of  America and I don't want to excuse the  partisanship as merely sensible because  of this precipice we might be  approaching part of the reason we have  this partisanship is because of partisan  media including the existence of Fox  News and other right-wing media carrying  water in a way that doesn't relate to  the facts on the ground at all social  media echo chambers like there are some  really toxic reasons why we have such  partisanship that even though the  country has moved to the left a lot of  money is still raised by the right by  kind of hunkering down these extremist  reactionary positions on abortion and  immigrants and so on and so forth  so there's a lot of really horrible  reasons why we have partisanship but  also our system rewards partisanship  if you run centrist campaigns it becomes  harder to raise money for re-election  because you're not appealing to the  people who are most radical and I use  that term non-judgmentally when it comes  to issues  radical positions justify and encourage  more donations and that's part of the  system that we have but to some degree  the election of Donald Trump was insane  and now there is a question are are we  real acting Trump and saying Trump was  not an anomaly or an anomaly depending  on which pronunciation you like we are  we've had four years of Trump and we're  going to four more that would be a huge  thing for the country to do on the other  hand we have the possibility of electing  the most progressive presidents in the  history of the United States Bernie  Sanders or Elizabeth Warren even some of  the other candidates would be more  progressive than anyone else who has  been president so far so I believe that  the hyper partisanship in part is also  because of this precipice of possible  significant change that we're going to  have the media fomented the media  profits from it no question about it and  we are living in two different realities  Media foments that in part the Internet  is a huge part of it you have everything  from militant conspiracy theorists more  and more white supremacy far-right hyper  nationalist types there is increasingly  a lack of middle ground represented in  media social media reinforces more and  more extreme versions of whatever it is  that you believe or support and it's  extraordinarily powerful getting through  to people and saying let's be sensible  becomes difficult and often not rewarded  when when you look at polls about what  TV shows what podcasts what websites the  left and the right are looking at they  are very different and they are  increasingly ones that merely reinforce  and continue to radicalize that  pre-existing worldview so serious  division has many negative effects both  sides can be more easily controlled by a  minority of their side by picking the  issues that will most catalyze and  rational and a reactionary create  reactionary views and that can be done  in perpetuity to keep increasing the  division or partisanship the deepening  political divide can also lead to  violence we've talked about how many of  us believe if Donald Trump were to be  removed from office by losing in 2020  but claimed that it was unfair that it  was rigged in some way I fear that there  would be violence and hyper-partisanship  and division can also cause that but I  don't believe the country is so much  divided as it is hyper partisan which  comes with its own set of issues what do  you think is the country divided  hyper-partisan a little bit of both one  or the other I want to hear from you
 

